(footprint "BAT_BH-18650-A5BJ001-2D"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "9.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "MYOUNG BH-18650-A5BJ001-2D single-cell 18650 holder, THM horizontal, DIP 90deg type. LCSC C19184083. Land pattern per MYOUNG drawing WD-CP-0336 rev A/0 (2023-09-08) 'PCB Layout Diagram': 2-dia2.5 terminal holes at 72.3 +/-0.8 mm pitch, 2-dia3.0 housing-boss holes at 55.5 +/-0.8 mm pitch, body 77.8 +/-0.8 x 20.8 +/-0.5 mm, housing height 21.5 +/-0.5 mm. Terminals are 0.3 mm steel, 1.53 mm wide, Ni-plated; housing is ABS (the Keystone 1043P it replaces was UL94V-0 PBT - this part carries no flame rating on the drawing). Dielectric 500 VAC 1 min, -10 to +100 C.\nREPLACES KEYSTONE 1043P. Terminal pitch 72.3 vs the Keystone's 72.22, so each terminal moves only 0.04 mm. POLARITY IS MIRRORED: this part marks POSITIVE at the pin-1 / -X end where the Keystone had P at +X, so BT2 is rotated 180 deg from the old orientation. It is also NOT polarized mechanically - unlike the 1043P's button-top dimple, nothing stops a reversed cell. It stands 21.5 mm off the board against the Keystone's 14.86 mm: CHECK ENCLOSURE CLEARANCE.\nTerminal pads drawn 3.4 mm (0.45 mm annular ring) rather than the vendor library's 3.1 mm (0.30 mm, right at JLCPCB's minimum), because a battery holder takes cell-insertion force. The two 3.0 mm boss holes are NPTH here; the vendor library wrongly made them plated pads with zero annular ring. Courtyard covers max material condition (78.6 x 21.3) plus 0.25 mm.")
	(tags "battery holder 18650 THM through-hole MYOUNG BH-18650-A5BJ001-2D C19184083")
